{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1071039-idigam","id":1071039,"title":"Idigam","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-03-30T21:53:09-07:00","id":1071039,"title":"Idigam","content":"So, I read <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/moon-banished/\" target=\"_blank\">this</a> and noticed that there is a whole lot of overlap available between Abyssal spirits and Idigam. In fact, the only space I am spotting that there wouldn't be is that Abyssal stuff can't be really true (but, given the Lie conceit, that <i>doesn't</i> mean it's not represented in the fallen world) and that Idigam weren't or aren't but could, theoretically, be. Also, idigam were bound moonside and hate werewolves while abyssal stuff generally is assumed not to care, overmuch.<br /> <br /> The differences are subtle enow that an enterprising storyteller may well decide none exist.<br /> <br /> It occurs that they could be handled as a strange form of Bound that was imprisoned on the moon by werewolves instead of Atlantis.<br /> <br /> (I ran a game in oWoD that had an abyssal spirit that acted very much like this, oddly enough.)<br /> <br /> <br /> The only gotcha with this interpretation I'm seeing is that their fluid nature requires that they lean on something real which sounds more Lower Depthsy than Abyssal. ('Course, there <i>is</i> a lot of overlap twixt those two, also.)<br /> <br /> <br /> Has anybody played around with using Idigam as a major Mage antagonist? Thoughts on story hooks/quirks with magic could be fun to discuss.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Grump, grouse, and/or gripe.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/672-thenate","name":"thenate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar672_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-30T22:03:32-07:00","id":1071050,"title":"","content":"No play experience, but I do suspect the idigam can throw one hell of a curve ball to any Spirit mage who thinks they know it all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-30T22:19:55-07:00","id":1071058,"title":"","content":"Well I consider myself more a Mage player than a werewolf player, but I do like the idea of making the Abyss a more encroaching threat on <i>all </i>gamelines, so I did entertain the idea of the Idigam being abyssal in some fashion. However, the Idigam are far more interesting when you keep them as Lovecraftian horrors, so they should be hard to understand, even to Mages.<br /> <br /> The most important thing I would establish first is that any Mage who is trying to tackle the Idigam is going to be getting into werewolf territory, so they either need to ally themselves with the werewolves or be prepared to spurn them and get on their bad side--which is not smart.<br /> <br /> You can throw <i>all</i> the potential answers to what Idigam <i>are</i> and keep Mages distracted or arguing about it except for the PC's, who either require werewolf help to get a better understanding of the Idigam, or at least a fighting chance.<br /> <br /> And the other thing I wanna mention is that the Idigam might actually be real, genuine, of this reality spirits--not abyssal at all. They can seem that way, but even gulmoths and acamoth tend to stay as one thing when they appear. They're manifestations of a lie, so they're corruptive of the nature they'd normally represent.<br /> <br /> Idigam are not like this. They're spirits of concepts that cannot or no longer exist. In Mage lore they could be <i>victims</i> of Exarchal nonsense from the time before, perhaps even surviving spirits of the time before that only existed in deep space.<br /> <br /> They can also be void spirits, spirits not of the abyss, but just proper spatial void. A spirit that formed in deep space with nothing around it from stray essence floating through space. Like if quanta essence of stars, but from stars that hold different resonance, collided in space enough times and formed a spirit, but it has nothing around to resonate with so it becomes a spirit of nothing. It isn't from the abyss, but it is <i>like</i> the abyss because of its unfortunate creation.<br /> <br /> If you want to mage it up even further, you could have them be a bizarre entity that can be both from the shadow <i>and</i> the astral realms---a spirit of the sidereal wastes that came out of the astral in the actual deep space that this former goetia originated from. Being a goetia in the Shadow of deep space invariably twists it into a shadow-spirit with no known resonance, driving it alien and mad and drifting to space until it hits our neck of the woods... enter werewolves (or mages). Or it is captured by Luna.<br /> <br /> But with that in mind, do try to make sure that Mages are interested in the antagonists from other gamelines with hubris in mind. Idigam are not a Mage thing, so when Mages take interest, it is due to an Obsession, and Obsessions = hijinks and trouble. Always remember the Hubris aspect.<br /> <br /> In fact the only gameline I think has more clout to be all-encompassing is probably Demon. Hell Demon even has this weird thing where apparently the Strix know about Infrastructure and mess with it, and it is implied a few times that the God-Machine uses the abyss as some sort of fuel source occassionally.<br /> <br /> Demon also has a <i>fascinating</i> idea that Idigam are somehow aborted god-machines, creating this weird dilemna where the God-Machine might be the Spirit of the Future and Idigam are Spirits-of-the-Past, such as before or during the formation of the Earth, or even from the Time Before.<br /> <br /> What if one, just one, idigam survived to the end of the universe and then traveled back in time to guarantee its own survival and omnipotence, becoming the God-Machine in the process. Probably has a sort of Durandal-esque survival scheme it is hatching. ((Durandal being a mad AI from the old Marathon games by Bungie---Durandal wants to survive the end of the universe)).<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7967-scarlet-witch","name":"Scarlet Witch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"498"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-30T23:07:56-07:00","id":1071083,"title":"","content":"There are some interesting points to ponder in there. Thanks. <br /> <br /> One thing I was considering is that, since the werewolf don't really know anything meaningful about Idigam, (Just the history of: Wolf locked them on the Moon whenever they got caught and they rock the world whenever they break loose and then vamoose and now you know the plot.) the werewolves hunt down mystics of various stripes, magi included, looking for answers. The scale of the havoc is such that I have to imagine that hubris wouldn't let many mages ignore the things. <br /> <br /> If they are abyssal (whether by direct source or sympathy) I could see some of them being prone to corrupting <i>mana</i> as well as essence. That'd be a bit inconvenient. Boost paradox? That seems plausible as a Numen.<br /> <br /> <br /> Hadn't read the Demon bit at all. That's a rather odd idea. <br /> <br /> I need to sleep. I'ma call it a night, here.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Grump, grouse, and/or gripe.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/672-thenate","name":"thenate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar672_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-31T00:11:38-07:00","id":1071105,"title":"","content":"Those would be very unusual wolves. Werewolves take care of themselves, are very pack oriented. They're a little bit xenophobic. It would also depend on what the design of the werewolves are--if they're partial to Wisdom renown, maybe, but if your werewolf pack are Glory or Honor renown focused, then they're going to refuse or even compete with mages to take down the idigam before the mages do.<br /> <br /> Werewolves might know more about the Idigam than you think too. In-fact, if your scenario focuses on mage characters, it is more interesting for them to know less than the werewolves. If you are running a more werewolf focused game, it is more interesting if the mages know more but want to be unhelpful--like the only mages who know the info you need are either Mad, Scelesti, or Seers! Perhaps even Banishers! No bueno!<br /> <br /> The werewolves in either case need a <i>good reason</i> for helping Mages, especially if they're going to play second fiddle.<br /> <br /> Have fun solving this idea!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7967-scarlet-witch","name":"Scarlet Witch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"498"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-31T07:52:10-07:00","id":1071252,"title":"","content":"Scarlet Witch has mostly got it, but it's entirely possible for a werewolf pack to have a mage or several mages in it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 03-31-2017, 10:56 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-31T08:26:03-07:00","id":1071264,"title":"","content":"While the design space that abyssal entities and idigam share is the same, namely that of &quot;out of context serious threat&quot; the key difference in their themes are evident as well. Idigam are spirits, therefore they're hungry. They have a purpose: to evolve, to become &quot;natural&quot;. This is never an abyssal entity's purpose. It knows it's very essence is the stuff of unreality (basically what fills Trump's mind when he designs policy)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-31T08:33:57-07:00","id":1071270,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scarlet Witch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1071039-idigam?p=1071105#post1071105\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Those would be very unusual wolves. Werewolves take care of themselves, are very pack oriented. They're a little bit xenophobic. It would also depend on what the design of the werewolves are--if they're partial to Wisdom renown, maybe, but if your werewolf pack are Glory or Honor renown focused, then they're going to refuse or even compete with mages to take down the idigam before the mages do.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't really agree. Pretty much everything we've seen of the Idigam presents them as existential threats to Uratha that can rip through entire packs easily. The Uratha need pretty much any advantage they can get. That essentially leaves only the unusual Uratha as eveyone else tends to end up dead.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-31T10:10:50-07:00","id":1071306,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1071039-idigam?p=1071270#post1071270\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't really agree. Pretty much everything we've seen of the Idigam presents them as existential threats to Uratha that can rip through entire packs easily. The Uratha need pretty much any advantage they can get. That essentially leaves only the unusual Uratha as eveyone else tends to end up dead.</div> </div> </div> </div>Unfortunately, mages are just as vulnerable, and bringing outsiders in only to have their soul ripped out and become heralds of the idigam would be a bad idea.<br /> <br /> Uratha have their own sources of information they're likely to seek out in this regard. But having an idigam as a mage antagonist would work fine.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-31T16:19:17-07:00","id":1071480,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1071039-idigam?p=1071252#post1071252\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Scarlet Witch has mostly got it, but it's entirely possible for a werewolf pack to have a mage or several mages in it.</div> </div> </div> </div>It is funny you should say that. The reason I have the opinion that I do is that the game I play in is a werewolf-mage crossover, and this was the kind of difficulty I went through during my prelude to join the pack.<br /> But yes, I think they would not trust mages very much, not because purely they're mages, but because they're mostly not in the pack. But if they let you <i>into</i> the pack, or at least the periphery, you're good.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1071039-idigam?p=1071270#post1071270\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't really agree. Pretty much everything we've seen of the Idigam presents them as existential threats to Uratha that can rip through entire packs easily. The Uratha need pretty much any advantage they can get. That essentially leaves only the unusual Uratha as eveyone else tends to end up dead.</div> </div> </div> </div>I still think they have their pride. If the Idigam became a danger to mages, or if an Uratha pack felt that they were and convinced a few mages as such, I could see that. But they'd still rather work with mages they know they can trust, which means they're either packmates or with a pack that another pack is allied with. The last thing they're going to want is for mages to give cursory help, wait for the werewolves to triumph but come back weakened, and then get shafted.<br /> <br /> Or not! I mean it's a storytelling game so if the story is about disparate groups coming together then that's great! And if there is a major threat that is on the cusp of victory against the Uratha, then it seems only logical that they'd branch out for help. I mean why wouldn't they? Their survival is on the line, it is stupid not to go for help! Or maybe it isn't. Perhaps that's only how a mage would think, and not a werewolf. Pride purity honor or maybe explicit orders from one or more Lunes to settle this themselves, perhaps there are werewolves who cannot or will not go to Mages because this is <i>their </i>fight, and any Mage who disagrees just doesn't get it. And any Mage that can earn their respect or become part of the pack will be the exception.<br /> <br /> Exploring all those options would just make things even more interesting though. One pack wants mages help, the other pack shuns their previous allies, or if they were rivals, uses this as an excuse to escalate the rivalry. What if the pack that wants mage help accidentally approaches the Seers, and then a Pentacle cabal finds out and tries to intervene before this backlashes against the werewolves?<br /> <br /> Perhaps the opposite. The Seers could see the Idigam as a threat to their mundane world of lies, and help for pragmatic reasons, but utilize whatever loyalty they get from the werewolves to try and gain an advantage against the Pentacle.<br /> <br /> I still think most Uratha would want to keep Mages at an arms distance and take on the Idigam themselves (especially since I doubt the Mages know very much about the Idigam either unless they're an Archmage...?), but no doubt <i>not </i>doing that can create some interesting stories too.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7967-scarlet-witch","name":"Scarlet Witch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"498"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-03T03:35:08-07:00","id":1072428,"title":"","content":"There's a whole category of Idigam whose ban and bane are humanity focused. And it turns out mages are just that chewy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}